  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
   "The schematic image was not available, so the wiring follows the text: a 2N7000 level shifter between the 3.3 V board and the 5 V NeoPixel ring. The board's pin 6 goes to the 2N7000 source, the board's 3.3 V (VCC) goes to the gate, and the drain goes to the ring DIN and, through the 10k resistor, to 5 V. The ring is powered from the 5 V and GND rails.",
   "The catalogue entry for the MKR GSM 1400 lists no digital pin ports, so I used 'D6' for the data pin. The pin number 6 is an assumption, as the manual does not state it.",
   "2N7000 is a TO-92 part, so I placed it in neighbouring holes of one row in the order S, G, D (columns 10, 11, 12). That follows the standard 2N7000 pinout, not the catalogue's TO-220 card.",
   "The catalogue lists no negative port on the MKR board for the LiPo battery, so only the battery + to BAT is recorded. The battery's - side is implied by the JST connector.",
   "The breadboard has no board-mounted headers. The MKR board is off-breadboard and connected by jumper wires.",
   "The micro USB cable has no ports, so the edge to the board's USB port has no port on the cable side.",
   "The antenna and SIM card are not in the parts list and are not modelled."
  ]
 },
